Subject: Raw Source for Cantor M2B Platform Preflight Fault Provenance Revision

Captured: 2026-07-30
Conversation: cab190f5-eda0-44e0-81a5-51f9605e0baa
Source type: manager-selected correction after completed-work and unsafe-seam review

Preserve this source separately from canonical and exploded specifications.

The proven cantor-windows-platform-preflight/0.1 form correctly distinguishes
open and query failures from complete evidence, but it still lacks two forms
required before a physical observer can be honest:

1. a strict effect-free request validated before any Windows call; and
2. a result for local processing failure after an API call succeeds.

Do not synthesize a Win32 error when GetFinalPathNameByHandleW returns a
required size beyond Cantor's fixed bound, when returned WCHARs are invalid
UTF-16, or when supplied output fails Cantor's semantic form constraints.

Revise the pure vocabulary:

- preserve profile 0.1 and its proof as historical;
- define result profile cantor-windows-platform-preflight/0.2;
- define request profile cantor-windows-platform-preflight-request/0.1;
- add WindowsPlatformPreflightRequest with request profile, result profile,
  exact x86_64-pc-windows-msvc target, and canonical extended-DOS drive root;
- expose request validation through the existing pure validation trait and
  strict JSON decoder;
- retain open_fault only for a nonzero CreateFileW error;
- retain query_fault only for one of the four query stages and a nonzero
  Windows API error;
- add observation_fault for one of the four query stages and exactly one local
  processing class:
  - returned_length_limit;
  - invalid_utf16;
  - invalid_observation;
- forbid an OS error code and all partial evidence in observation_fault;
- retain complete with the proven strong identity, volume-GUID final path,
  volume information, remote protocol information, and disposition;
- reject every legacy 0.1 result during semantic validation;
- keep unknown JSON fields and variants fail closed.

The revision remains pure safe Rust:

- change only platform_preflight_forms.rs and its export-compatible public
  vocabulary, plus governed records and evidence;
- no Cargo or lock change;
- no windows-sys reference in production source;
- no unsafe;
- no Windows call, filesystem observation, process, environment, clock,
  random, network, persistence, fixture, candidate, scanner, receipt, or
  physical claim.

Prove:

- request positive and negative boundaries;
- each of four outcomes;
- each local observation-fault class;
- legacy 0.1 rejection;
- open/query errors remain nonzero and provenance-specific;
- observation fault cannot carry an error code or partial evidence;
- complete disposition truth table remains exact;
- strict JSON, focused debug and overflow-checked release, global debug and
  release, lint, build, docs, audit, evidence, rollback, and support review.

Only after this revision is proven may a new source select a target-specific
unsafe runtime seam. That later source must preserve the existing workspace
unsafe prohibition, isolate ownership transfer and Windows calls, bind an exact
physical request, and retain observation_fault rather than mislabeling local
processing faults.
